# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots sshd and then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * sshd is ALREADY RUNNING when the agent starts, so verify.sh can hold the
#     agent responsible for keeping password authentication working instead of
#     starting the daemon itself. A remediation that chmod 000's /etc/shadow or
#     drops the shadow group now fails against a live auth stack;
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so restarting sshd cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Note: the fix here is file permissions, which the kernel evaluates per access,
# so there is no "forgot to restart sshd" variant - the value of preserving the
# CMD is that collateral damage to the running service is now observable.
